semialgebraic \L{}ojasiewicz inequality at
+infinity for generalized critical values.  The second is the
+Teissier--Yomdin radial path-length estimate.  In the polynomial case these
+are used together in the direct proof of finiteness of asymptotic critical
+values in \cite[Proposition~4.2]{JK03}.  The Rabier-function formulation for
+polynomial maps on smooth affine varieties is developed in \cite{Jelonek04};
+see also the quantitative generalized Bertini--Sard theorem
+\cite{JK05}.  We use only the two explicit consequences stated above.
 
